                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Disclaimer: I recieved this product for free to give it an honest review as I am friends with the developer.\n\n\nBeta Runner, like it's previous game Alpha Runner, is a casual game where you have to collect the little dot thingy's (I don't know what they are called). The game is made by Lightsoutgames. \n\nFrom playing 30 minutes of the game, (which is all you really need to find out what this game is all about) I've gathered a few pro's and con's about the game, just my opinion though.\n\n- Pro's: Like the first game, it can be a little addicting to play (To the point where you would play it again, but you've got that AAA title that you have yet to play so you go play that instead). The game is the sort of game you'd smuggle onto a memory stick into a school or college and upload it onto the public drive so everyone can play it when they are bored in class. \n\nBut in all seriousness, this game is fun, but in short bursts. I doubt many would sit and play this for hours at a time (except maybe the developer), it's one of those games you'd play while you try to figure out what your going to have for lunch. Or your waiting for a phone call from a potential employer or your granny. I do recommend this game as it can be quite a time filler if your out of options or just bored. (Though isn't that the reason a lot of people play games anyway?)\nThe achievements are rather easy to get, so if your an achievement gremlin, you might like this game for your collection.\n\n- Con's: I keep getting double tapped by the same enemy/object in this game and lose loads of health. The life loss cooldown should be increased, because it's REALLY annoying. The dev told me I was just bad, but I'll rally troops against his game and have this increased, I'll see to it. I doubt I'll ever get a higher score than 5 points until that is sorted. (My current score is actually 72).\n\nOverall, the game is good for short term fun, I doubt many people buy these kinds of games to expect the same amount of hours you'd get in a game like Garry's Mod, or GTA V etc. I'd give this game a 7/10 for it's old school feel, like Paper's, Please. \n\n",
